load("@komira//tools/build/mojo:defs.bzl", "mojo_library")

# The Parquet reader core. These parts hold the value decoders of the Parquet
# encodings: PLAIN (plain, with FIXED_LEN_BYTE_ARRAY in plain_flba), RLE /
# Bit-Packing Hybrid (rle, with its bit-unpack kernels in rle_bitunpack),
# DELTA_BINARY_PACKED (delta), DELTA_LENGTH_BYTE_ARRAY and DELTA_BYTE_ARRAY
# (delta_byte_array) and BYTE_STREAM_SPLIT (byte_stream_split); the DECIMAL to
# Decimal128 decoders (decimal_decode); the RLE_DICTIONARY decoder
# (dictionary, with its gathers in dictionary_resolve and dict_gather_fused)
# and the definition-level bitmap (def_level_bitmap); the Dremel level helpers
# (nested); the column decoder's type map and array helpers (decode_helpers,
# null_expand); and the run-time arms and fire counters of the decode and scan
# paths (decode_arm_trace, scan_copy_trace, payload_sel_trace,
# staged_filter_trace); and the row-selection gathers: the (skip, select)
# intervals of a filter mask (selection_vector), their shared page records
# (gather_common), and the gathers of selected rows out of PLAIN BYTE_ARRAY
# pages (gather_byte_array) and dictionary-encoded pages (gather_dict). Every
# public decoder takes Spans; the arms are set by setters, never by the
# environment.
# They also read a file's footer and metadata: the file reader over any
# FileSystem (file_reader), the Thrift Compact reader (thrift_compact), the
# footer parsers (metadata_parser, footer_header), the page header parser
# (page_header_parser), bloom filters and the row-group bloom pruner
# (bloom_reader, bloom_pruner), a row-count cache (num_rows_cache) and the
# partition-predicate mapping (partition_pred_bridge).
#
# It also reads a file's footer: the file reader over any FileSystem
# (file_reader), the Thrift Compact reader (thrift_compact), the footer
# parsers (metadata_parser, footer_header), the page header parser
# (page_header_parser), bloom filters and the row-group bloom pruner
# (bloom_reader, bloom_pruner), a row-count cache (num_rows_cache) and the
# partition-predicate mapping (partition_pred_bridge). The column chunk page
# walk in front of the selection gathers (gather) joins the two: it parses
# page headers, decompresses the selected pages (komira_parquet_codec) and
# gathers their selected rows.
#
# It also decodes column chunks a chunk of rows at a time into a reused
# buffer (subrg_column_cursor, with its page helpers in subrg_cursor_pages and
# its counters in subrg_dbp_trace and subrg_scan_route_trace), holds a
# worker's reusable decode buffers (column_decode_context), decodes a nested
# leaf with its levels (nested_decoder) and reads one PLAIN page from a file
# range (column_reader).
#
# And it decodes a whole flat column chunk into one column (column_decoder,
# its steps in column_decoder_state, _pages, _values, _assemble, _finish and
# _strings, and the dense-string rebuild counter in dict_mat_counter). The
# page CRC is the standard CRC-32, from komira_zlib.
#
# It decides from a footer what a scan needs to read: the row-group pruner on
# min/max statistics and its all-match dual (rg_pruner), row selections and
# their page clip (row_selection), the row groups a table-scale row window
# overlaps (row_window) and the Arrow types an `ARROW:schema` footer key
# names (arrow_schema_hint); and it reads a column chunk as stored for a
# pass-through write (bypass).
#
# It keeps a session's parsed footers, by path, with their preambles and a
# pinned whole-file mapping, revalidated by stat on each shared hit
# (runtime_footer_cache, within the pin budget of footer_pin_budget), and
# serves a footer's statistics as TableStats and as a StatsProvider
# (table_stats).
#
# It reads a local file a row group or a morsel at a time
# (morsel_reader, its morsel windows in morsel_slice, the data-page count of
# the one-pass selection decode in data_page_count), and decodes a row group
# from bytes the caller already holds, with no I/O (bytes_decode). Each
# column chunk decoded there is counted (komira_counters).
#
# The welded tests:
# - test_rle_simd, test_rle_simd_bw_small: bit-packed runs at every bit width
#   the SIMD kernels specialize, and the dedicated bw=1/2/4 byte paths, at
#   counts on and off the SIMD lane boundaries, against a test-local encoder.
# - test_def_levels_u8: the per-page u8 validity vector from RLE def levels.
# - test_delta_byte_array: DELTA_LENGTH_BYTE_ARRAY and DELTA_BYTE_ARRAY round
#   trips and the DataPage V2 header parse.
# - test_partition_pred_bridge_roundtrip: the partition-predicate mapping
#   round-trips every op losslessly.
# - test_neon_bss_decode: the SIMD BYTE_STREAM_SPLIT decode against the
#   scalar block-transpose reference, f32 and f64, with and without a tail.
# - test_parquet_encoding: PLAIN, RLE and DELTA_BINARY_PACKED decodes of
#   hand-encoded pages with known values.
# - test_int96_decode: INT96 timestamps (Julian day + nanos) to Unix nanos.
# - test_plain_ba_fused_byte_equiv: the two PLAIN BYTE_ARRAY walks emit the
#   same bytes and refuse the same pages; the fused walk allocates no more;
#   a dictionary page decode reaches the gated walk.
# - test_plain_ba_raise_outlined: the walks' refusal sentences, byte for byte.
# - test_flba_decimal_simd_parity: the SIMD FLBA DECIMAL to Float64 decode
#   against a scalar reference, FLBA(16) and FLBA(8), with tails, and the
#   dictionary decoder's FLBA(16) resolve against the same reference.
# - test_string_share_byte_equiv: Column.from_string_shared against the
#   copying Column.from_string, and the paired string share counters.
# - test_dict_gather_simd_parity, test_dictionary_resolve_int32_simd_parity,
#   test_dictionary_resolve_int64_simd_parity,
#   test_dictionary_resolve_float64_simd_parity: DictionaryDecoder.resolve_*
#   against a scalar gather, over dictionary sizes and counts on and off the
#   SIMD step and the prefetch distance.
# - test_nested_types: leaf levels of flat, struct, list, map and Dremel-paper
#   schemas, and struct, list and map columns rebuilt from their levels.
# - test_flat_read_types_are_never_nested: the type map never yields a nested
#   Arrow type, swept over every physical type and annotation, and the
#   read path's column copier refuses a nested column.
# - test_selection_interval: SelectionInterval from a mask (runs, gaps,
#   coalescing across 64-bit words), the totals and the index fallback.
# - test_gather_byte_array: the PLAIN BYTE_ARRAY selection gathers against a
#   positional reference (empty, short and long values, several pages, many
#   selections, nullable), and malformed pages refused on both walk legs.
# - test_gather_fixed_width_direct: the PLAIN fixed-width gathers, non-null
#   and nullable, every type and walk shape against a positional reference,
#   and their refusals.
# - test_gather_fixed_width_non_null: the non-null fixed-width gather on
#   hand-built pages (one page, several, page edges, no interval).
# - test_gather_column_direct: the column chunk page walk on chunks it
#   gathers (PLAIN and dictionary, every type, codec, page kind, mask and
#   annotation), with page headers written from parquet.thrift.
# - test_gather_column_fallbacks_direct: the chunks it hands back (None) and
#   the refusals it raises.
# - test_subrg_cursor_dict_direct: ResumableColumnCursor on dictionary chunks:
#   codes in fills of every size equal the codes written, exactly
#   min(max_rows, rows left) per call, a long RLE run split across calls,
#   numeric and string dictionaries, OPTIONAL pages with and without a null,
#   a bit-width-0 page, seek_to_row ranges, the data-pages-only open, and the
#   chunks refused at open (counted) or mid-decode.
# - test_subrg_cursor_flat_direct: the cursor on flat chunks: PLAIN values
#   copied in fills or read in place by grains that stop at page ends,
#   DELTA_BINARY_PACKED values carried across fills of every size, row-range
#   seeks by byte offset and by decode-skip, the DBP counters, and refusals
#   (V2, BYTE_STREAM_SPLIT, a short PLAIN page, a small buffer).
# - test_subrg_admit_all_pages_direct: the cursor's whole-chunk page header
#   walk, one test per refusal case against an admitted control.
# - test_subrg_traces_direct: the DBP and scan route counters, grains, the
#   power-of-two milestones and the print gate.
# - test_column_decode_context_direct: the reusable buffers grow and never
#   shrink, band slots and row-group dictionaries, the band resolve refusing
#   a code outside its dictionary, band cursors and the in-place grain view.
# - test_nested_decoder_direct: decode_column_with_levels: list<int32>
#   levels and values over V1 and V2 pages, every codec and type, dictionary
#   codes at their bit width, strings across pages, a numeric dictionary
#   spill, and the malformed chunks it refuses.
# - test_column_reader_local: PLAIN pages read from a local file, stored and
#   SNAPPY, and the reader's refusals.
# - test_column_decoder_direct: decode_column_pages on hand-encoded chunks:
#   the single PLAIN page moved or copied (and a DECIMAL one as Decimal128),
#   nullable V1 pages, V2 pages with bare RLE definition levels, BOOLEAN,
#   INT96, FIXED_LEN_BYTE_ARRAY with nulls, DELTA_BINARY_PACKED (and a short
#   page refused), both BYTE_STREAM_SPLIT arms and their counters,
#   DELTA_LENGTH_BYTE_ARRAY and DELTA_BYTE_ARRAY pages all kept, the page
#   CRC-32 (a flipped byte and a CRC-32C refused), and malformed chunks.
# - test_column_decoder_dict_direct: dictionary chunks: strings kept or
#   rebuilt dense (dict_mat_counter), numbers resolved, kept, or decoded into
#   the reused codes buffer across chunks, checked codes for the fused count,
#   dictionary-to-PLAIN switches (kept in order, or refused), the all-null
#   dictionary chunk, and the dictionaries refused.
# - test_column_decoder_pyarrow: every chunk of five pyarrow-written files
#   (komira_parquet_codec's fixtures, staged at parquet/): ZSTD V2 pages with
#   CRCs and nulls, dictionaries over several SNAPPY pages, GZIP PLAIN,
#   INT96, zero rows; and a flipped byte refused by a real page's CRC.
# - test_rg_pruner_direct: the min/max pruner and its all-match dual on
#   footers built as structs: every operator on both sides, signed and
#   unsigned integers, floats (no prune on !=), byte arrays, AND and OR,
#   names resolved among the top-level leaves after a group, DECIMAL and the
#   other conservative cases, the null trap and the file-level count.
# - test_row_selection_direct: RowSelection operations against a per-row
#   bitmap over generated selections, nulls in a mask, selects_all and the
#   cursor's phases.
# - test_row_window_direct: the row-group window, hand cases and a sweep
#   against a brute-force answer.
# - test_arrow_schema_hint_direct: ARROW:schema values made by the IPC
#   encoder, both framings, unreadable values, the key lookup and the guard.
# - test_bypass_direct: a chunk's bytes read as stored, its start at a
#   leading dictionary page, its leaf name after a group, and the refusals.
# - test_runtime_footer_cache_direct: the footer cache on files written by
#   the test: parse once, shared footers and one pin, revalidation of a
#   rewritten or freshly written file, the pin budget, invalidate, the
#   row-count memo, the stripped footer and summary, a file system that is
#   not mmap-backed, and the budget policy.
# - test_table_stats_direct: the eager fold and the provider: bounds decoded
#   by type (unsigned, UINT_64 past Int64.MAX, DECIMAL), top-level leaves,
#   HLL register merge against one sketch over the union, the path entry
#   points.
# - test_morsel_reader_direct: ParquetMorselReader on files written by
#   komira_test_parquet_file: morsels per row group and cut across row groups
#   and pages at unaligned rows (validity rebased), one-row morsels, reset,
#   a file of no rows, a kept dictionary through morsel windows, projections
#   and the decode census (one count per row group and column, never per
#   morsel), the shared decodes with and without the buffer move, the
#   one-pass selection decode, raw chunks against the file's bytes, the
#   footer cache, and the refusals.
# - test_bytes_decode_direct: the I/O-free entry points on the same kind of
#   file: the row group's byte range exactly its chunks, every row group
#   decoded from its own bytes (projection, kept dictionary, census), one
#   chunk out of the whole file, INT64 and nullable INT32 dictionary codes
#   mapped back to the rows (PLAIN and BYTE_ARRAY chunks get None), and the
#   refusals.
# - test_no_env_reads: the package's sources read no environment, import no
#   komira package outside the deps below (and never komira_core), hold no
#   raw pointer in a public signature, rebuild no address from an integer
#   and name no wildcard origin. It is staged every source `srcs` compiles,
#   so a module the scan does not read fails it.
_SRCS = glob(["**/*.mojo"], exclude = ["tests/**/*.mojo"])

_PYARROW_FIXTURES = [
    "pyarrow_gzip_plain.parquet",
    "pyarrow_int96_ts.parquet",
    "pyarrow_multi_dict_page.parquet",
    "pyarrow_page_crc_zstd_v2.parquet",
    "pyarrow_zero_row.parquet",
]

mojo_library(
    name = "komira_parquet",
    srcs = _SRCS,
    deps = [
        "//src/komira_arrow:komira_arrow",
        "//src/komira_arrow_ipc:komira_arrow_ipc",
